{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 1, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a compelling and intense film that delves into the early days of facebook and the complex character of mark zuckerberg. the movie, directed by david fincher, is based on the true story of how the world's largest social media platform was created. it is a story of ambition, genius, and the cost of success, with a focus on the legal battles and personal relationships that shaped zuckerberg's path.\n\nthe film's narrative structure is non-linear, jumping between various timelines and legal depositions, which adds to the sense of complexity and tension. this approach effectively portrays the chaotic and often controversial nature of the story, as well as the ethical dilemmas that zuckerberg faced. the script, written by Aaron Sorkin, is sharp and witty, with dialogue that is both thought-provoking and engaging.\n\nthe performances in the social network are outstanding, particularly joshua perez's portrayal of mark zuckerberg. perez captures the character's brilliance, insecurity, and ruthlessness, making zuckerberg a deeply flawed but fascinating protagonist. the supporting cast is also strong, with andrew garfield and jesse Eisenberg delivering compelling performances as Eduardo Saverin and Sean Parker, respectively.\n\nvisually, the social network is a treat, with its stylish and modern cinematography capturing the essence of the tech world. the music, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is edgy and dynamic, perfectly complementing the film's tone.\n\nwhile the social network offers an intriguing look into the birth of facebook, it is not without its flaws. the film can be quite dense and requires the audience's full attention to keep up with its non-linear narrative. some viewers may find the legal disputes somewhat dry or the personal relationships underdeveloped.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-crafted and thought-provoking film that provides an engaging exploration of the tech industry, ambition, and the human cost of success. it is a must-watch for fans of biopics and tech dramas, and is a testament to the power of storytelling in bringing real-life events to the big screen.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.15858662128448486}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.007749966345727444}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -0.0004894727608188987}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.08163770288228989}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.16859997808933258}, {"token": " compelling", "logprob": -1.4621939659118652}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.8676386475563049}, {"token": " intense", "logprob": -1.444314956665039}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.47690123319625854}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.12615211308002472}, {"token": " delves", "logprob": -0.6196578741073608}, {"token": " into", "logprob": -0.05772450566291809}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0008217295398935676}, {"token": " early", "logprob": -1.621790885925293}, {"token": " days", "logprob": -0.02066767029464245}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.04903418570756912}, {"token": " face", "logprob": -0.011534903198480606}, {"token": "book", "logprob": -8.284702198579907e-05}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.029202472418546677}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.3035275638103485}, {"token": " complex", "logprob": -0.381197988986969}, {"token": " character", "logprob": -2.981778621673584}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.006552283186465502}, {"token": " mark", "logprob": -0.16120946407318115}, {"token": " z", "logprob": -0.04891454428434372}, {"token": "ucker", "logprob": -0.0003488647344056517}, {"token": "berg", "logprob": -2.2053474822314456e-05}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.2666904032230377}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.682171642780304}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -0.46864649653434753}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -2.318035125732422}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.024548480287194252}, {"token": "